Third-party components

PHIF automates the deployment of existing, separately-licensed hypervisor
storage integrations and depends on third-party open-source software, each
distributed under its own license. Notable runtime dependencies include:

  * FastAPI, Starlette, Uvicorn, Pydantic            (MIT / BSD)
  * SQLAlchemy, Alembic, psycopg                     (MIT / LGPL)
  * cryptography                                     (Apache-2.0 / BSD)
  * httpx, asyncssh, ansible-runner                  (BSD / Apache-2.0)
  * py-pure-client                                   (BSD-2-Clause)
  * pyvmomi                                          (Apache-2.0)
  * React, Vite, and the frontend toolchain          (MIT)

The HPE VM Essentials connector builds a Morpheus/VME storage plugin against
the morpheus-plugin-api, which is provided by the appliance at runtime and is
not redistributed by this project.

